\chapter{Changes from first edition}

A chapter (\ref{_watching_time_elapse}) was added to describe time.

The new \c{TimeoutArgument}, allowing absolute times to be used instead of \c{Timeout*} timeouts was explained.

The \ref{_enforcing_sub-object_bounds} section was added to document how the compiler can enforce bounds on address-taken structure fields.

The \ref{_using_permissions_on_software-defined_capabilities} section was added to document how user-defined capabilities work and are used.
These are used in the core RTOS by the heap allocator.
That use is now documented in \ref{_allocating_with_an_explicit_capability}, which includes an example of passing an allocation capability across a compartment boundary.
